<http://data.silknow.org/object/92d3ba7d-2122-33d1-a723-91cf26f0071b>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Dress fabric of woven silk, Iran, 1860-1899"@en , "Dress fabric of woven silk, twill binding and bias cut.\nA repeating pattern of two very narrow tooth edged stripes.\n[1] dark blue ground with isolated flowering plants in yellow and white in two colour variations with green or yellow leaves arranged in horizontal rows across the alternate stripes\n[2] white ground with separate diagonally placed leaves edged in blue and either green or yellow centres [two rows of yellow centres, then one row green, one row yellow, two rows green centres].\nWarp: white and blue silk.\nWeft: white, light green, yellow, pink silk, all Z-twist.\n\nTechnique possibly known as Hussain Kuli Khan."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/d07f967a-98a0-3fff-a6b1-e68d21e5ae37> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Dress fabric of woven silk, twill binding and bias cut.\nA repeating pattern of two very narrow tooth edged stripes.\n[1] dark blue ground with isolated flowering plants in yellow and white in two colour variations with green or yellow leaves arranged in horizontal rows across the alternate stripes\n[2] white ground with separate diagonally placed leaves edged in blue and either green or yellow centres [two rows of yellow centres, then one row green, one row yellow, two rows green centres].\nWarp: white and blue silk.\nWeft: white, light green, yellow, pink silk, all Z-twist.\n\nTechnique possibly known as Hussain Kuli Khan."@en , "Dress fabric of woven silk, Iran, 1860-1899"@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/92d3ba7d-2122-33d1-a723-91cf26f0071b/dimension/2> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/92d3ba7d-2122-33d1-a723-91cf26f0071b/dimension/1> ;
        dc:identifier                  "T.21:121-1955" ;
